*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Molecule: H2O (asymmetric geometry)
* Basis: 6-31G
* Symmetry: C1
* Features tested: Analytic SS- and SA-MC-PDFT gradients with a translated
*                  meta-GGA on-top functional (tM06-L)
* Responsible person: Bhavnesh Jangid, University of Chicago, 2026
* Comments: The analytic gradients were checked against central finite
*           differences of the MC-PDFT energy (steps 0.08-0.01 A, with
*           Richardson extrapolation); agreement is within 1e-5 Eh/bohr.
*           The RICD cases check the same gradients with Cholesky vectors.
*           Starting orbitals are the converged CAS(2,2) ones, to avoid the
*           saddle point reached from the SCF guess for this geometry.
*           The finite-difference comparison used the Fine grid; the coarse
*           grid is used here to keep the test cheap.
*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

